.vercel
.env*
# The one exception, and it must stay one: the documented, value-free template. `.env*` is otherwise
# deliberately broad — it is what stops a real `.env.local` being committed — so this negation is
# narrow and explicit rather than a relaxed pattern. Placeholders only in that file, ever.
!.env.example

# Incremental TypeScript build cache — a machine-local artifact that churns on every
# typecheck. Tracked by accident; it is not source and its diffs are noise.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Phase 1b local reconciliation tool — real bank/ledger data and generated reports never committed
# (financial exports/PII, same discipline as DB dumps — see PRODUCT_STANDARDS.md).
tools/reconciliation-phase1b/data/
tools/reconciliation-phase1b/output/
tools/reconciliation-phase1b/*.xlsx
__pycache__/
*.pyc
